It was originally planned to continue through

280
00:10:04,241 --> 00:10:06,472
the second quarter of twenty twenty-seven.

281
00:10:06,652 --> 00:10:09,513
One source said Hyundai had told suppliers

282
00:10:09,513 --> 00:10:12,375
it was cutting production by roughly half.

283
00:10:12,555 --> 00:10:15,229
Hyundai declined to confirm the report,

284
00:10:15,229 --> 00:10:17,697
saying it does not comment on future

285
00:10:17,697 --> 00:10:19,068
product speculation.

286
00:10:19,419 --> 00:10:21,142
Here is why it struggled,

287
00:10:21,142 --> 00:10:23,142
and it is a perfect lesson in

288
00:10:23,142 --> 00:10:23,970
competition.

289
00:10:24,150 --> 00:10:26,212
According to The Autopian,

290
00:10:26,212 --> 00:10:29,306
the Maverick outsold the Santa Cruz six

291
00:10:29,306 --> 00:10:29,862
to one.

292
00:10:30,042 --> 00:10:33,253
The Maverick gets thirty-eight miles per gallon

293
00:10:33,253 --> 00:10:36,532
combined, versus twenty-five for the Santa Cruz.

294
00:10:36,712 --> 00:10:38,578
Its bed is four and a half

295
00:10:38,578 --> 00:10:40,230
feet long, versus four.

296
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:43,328
And it started at twenty-nine thousand eight

297
00:10:43,328 --> 00:10:46,246
hundred forty dollars including destination,

298
00:10:46,246 --> 00:10:49,562
versus thirty-one thousand three hundred fifty for

299
00:10:49,562 --> 00:10:50,557
the Santa Cruz.

300
00:10:50,907 --> 00:10:53,848
So the Santa Cruz lost on almost

301
00:10:53,848 --> 00:10:56,882
every number a buyer cares about:

302
00:10:56,882 --> 00:10:59,916
price, fuel economy and bed size.

303
00:11:00,096 --> 00:11:02,135
The twist is that Hyundai does not

304
00:11:02,135 --> 00:11:03,335
see it as a failure.

305
00:11:03,515 --> 00:11:06,236
The company said the truck has helped

306
00:11:06,236 --> 00:11:09,545
it gain valuable experience and visibility in

307
00:11:09,545 --> 00:11:11,015
the open-bed market.

308
00:11:11,195 --> 00:11:14,400
And Hyundai says a new midsize body-on-frame

309
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:16,075
truck is due in the U S

310
00:11:16,075 --> 00:11:18,115
market before twenty thirty.

311
00:11:18,465 --> 00:11:21,078
Number six is the most talked-about truck

312
00:11:21,078 --> 00:11:21,971
of the decade.

313
00:11:22,151 --> 00:11:23,788
The Tesla Cybertruck.

314
00:11:23,968 --> 00:11:27,126
Revealed in twenty nineteen with stainless steel

315
00:11:27,126 --> 00:11:29,494
panels and a shape like nothing else

316
00:11:29,494 --> 00:11:30,284
on the road.

317
00:11:30,464 --> 00:11:32,823
Its first full year on the market

318
00:11:32,823 --> 00:11:34,468
was twenty twenty-four,

319
00:11:34,468 --> 00:11:38,044
and according to Cox Automotive estimates reported

320
00:11:38,044 --> 00:11:41,262
by InsideEVs, Tesla sold close to thirty-nine

321
00:11:41,262 --> 00:11:43,478
thousand Cybertrucks that year.

322
00:11:43,829 --> 00:11:45,094
Then the numbers turned.

323
00:11:45,274 --> 00:11:47,455
According to the same estimates,

324
00:11:47,455 --> 00:11:50,863
Americans bought about twenty thousand two hundred

325
00:11:50,863 --> 00:11:53,180
Cybertrucks in twenty twenty-five.

326
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:55,659
That is nearly half the previous year.

327
00:11:55,839 --> 00:11:57,755
And here is the gap that makes

328
00:11:57,755 --> 00:11:59,926
it a flop by Tesla's own standard.

329
00:12:00,106 --> 00:12:02,544
Tesla says it has the capacity to

330
00:12:02,544 --> 00:12:06,756
produce over one hundred twenty-five thousand Cybertrucks

331
00:12:06,756 --> 00:12:08,972
per year at its Texas factory,

332
00:12:08,972 --> 00:12:11,706
and Elon Musk has floated two hundred

333
00:12:11,706 --> 00:12:14,144
fifty thousand as a target in the

334
00:12:14,144 --> 00:12:14,514
past.

335
00:12:14,864 --> 00:12:16,025
Why did it fall?

336
00:12:16,205 --> 00:12:17,450
It was expensive,

337
00:12:17,450 --> 00:12:18,769
it was polarizing,

338
00:12:18,769 --> 00:12:21,334
and it arrived just as the electric

339
00:12:21,334 --> 00:12:22,799
truck market cooled.

340
00:12:22,979 --> 00:12:26,064
The federal tax credit for electric vehicles

341
00:12:26,064 --> 00:12:28,026
ended in twenty twenty-five,

342
00:12:28,026 --> 00:12:30,340
which hurt every electric pickup.

343
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:32,497
And the Cybertruck's design,

344
00:12:32,497 --> 00:12:34,969
the very thing that made it famous,

345
00:12:34,969 --> 00:12:38,148
also kept many traditional truck buyers away.

346
00:12:38,498 --> 00:12:39,902
Here is the twist.

347
00:12:40,082 --> 00:12:41,267
By some measures,

348
00:12:41,267 --> 00:12:43,705
the Cybertruck is not a total flop.

349
00:12:43,885 --> 00:12:46,594
Twenty thousand trucks in one year is

350
00:12:46,594 --> 00:12:49,523
more than many niche vehicles ever sell,

351
00:12:49,523 --> 00:12:52,378
and far more than the Lincoln Blackwood

352
00:12:52,378 --> 00:12:54,282
or the Chevy S S R managed

353
00:12:54,282 --> 00:12:55,820
in their whole lives.

354
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,106
It is a flop compared with its

355
00:12:58,106 --> 00:13:00,354
promise, not compared with zero.

356
00:13:00,534 --> 00:13:01,683
And that is the lesson.

357
00:13:01,863 --> 00:13:03,936
A truck can be judged a failure

358
00:13:03,936 --> 00:13:06,344
simply because it promised too much.

359
00:13:06,695 --> 00:13:09,421
Number seven is two trucks that represent

360
00:13:09,421 --> 00:13:11,815
the biggest truck bet of the decade.

361
00:13:11,995 --> 00:13:14,958
The Ford F-one-fifty Lightning and the Ram

362
00:13:14,958 --> 00:13:16,511
fifteen hundred R E V.

363
00:13:16,691 --> 00:13:19,318
Both were supposed to prove that electric

364
00:13:19,318 --> 00:13:21,497
full-size pickups were the future.

365
00:13:21,677 --> 00:13:23,965
One was cancelled before it was sold.

366
00:13:24,145 --> 00:13:26,461
The other was ended after three years

367
00:13:26,461 --> 00:13:27,337
of production.

368
00:13:27,688 --> 00:13:29,069
Start with the Ram.

369
00:13:29,249 --> 00:13:32,233
The all-electric Ram fifteen hundred R E

370
00:13:32,233 --> 00:13:34,322
V was delayed several times,

371
00:13:34,322 --> 00:13:37,007
and in September twenty twenty-five,

372
00:13:37,007 --> 00:13:40,663
Ram cancelled the battery-only version before the

373
00:13:40,663 --> 00:13:42,752
first customer received one.

374
00:13:42,932 --> 00:13:44,194
The name was kept,

375
00:13:44,194 --> 00:13:46,720
but moved to a range-extended truck,

376
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:49,456
where a gas engine charges the battery.

377
00:13:49,636 --> 00:13:52,338
The electric pickup Ram promised for years

378
00:13:52,338 --> 00:13:54,397
never reached a single driveway.

379
00:13:54,747 --> 00:13:55,583
Then the Lightning.

380
00:13:55,763 --> 00:13:57,729
According to Fox Business,

381
00:13:57,729 --> 00:13:59,393
on December sixteenth,

382
00:13:59,393 --> 00:14:03,250
twenty twenty-five, Ford announced a nineteen point

383
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:06,275
five billion dollar charge as it changed

384
00:14:06,275 --> 00:14:07,939
its electric strategy,

385
00:14:07,939 --> 00:14:11,796
and ended production of the all-electric Lightning.

386
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:14,956
In the third quarter of twenty twenty-six,

387
00:14:14,956 --> 00:14:16,873
according to autoevolution,

388
00:14:16,873 --> 00:14:20,421
Ford sold only two hundred eighty-nine Lightnings,

389
00:14:20,421 --> 00:14:23,046
compared with ten thousand and five a

390
00:14:23,046 --> 00:14:23,969
year earlier.

391
00:14:24,319 --> 00:14:25,851
Here is the twist.

392
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:28,771
The Lightning was not unpopular at first.

393
00:14:28,951 --> 00:14:30,994
It had long waiting lists when it

394
00:14:30,994 --> 00:14:31,552
launched.

395
00:14:31,732 --> 00:14:33,339
The problem was price,

396
00:14:33,339 --> 00:14:35,677
towing range, and the end of the

397
00:14:35,677 --> 00:14:36,480
tax credit.

398
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:39,145
And while the electric truck faded,

399
00:14:39,145 --> 00:14:42,836
Ford's hybrid F-one-fifty sold eighty-four thousand,

400
00:14:42,836 --> 00:14:46,598
nine hundred thirty-four units in twenty twenty-five,

401
00:14:46,598 --> 00:14:47,875
according to Ford.

402
00:14:48,055 --> 00:14:50,842
Buyers did not reject new technology.

403
00:14:51,022 --> 00:14:53,876
They rejected the technology that asked them

404
00:14:53,876 --> 00:14:55,109
to change too much.

405
00:14:55,459 --> 00:14:57,425
Before we look at the pattern,

406
00:14:57,425 --> 00:14:59,261
a few dishonorable mentions,

407
00:14:59,261 --> 00:15:01,424
trucks that did not flop as hard,

408
00:15:01,424 --> 00:15:04,178
but never reached what their makers hoped.

409
00:15:04,358 --> 00:15:07,233
The first is the Cadillac Escalade E

410
00:15:07,233 --> 00:15:09,469
X T, the rival that beat the

411
00:15:09,469 --> 00:15:10,267
Blackwood.

412
00:15:10,447 --> 00:15:12,342
According to SlashGear,

413
00:15:12,342 --> 00:15:15,225
it was unveiled in two thousand one

414
00:15:15,225 --> 00:15:18,191
and continued until twenty thirteen.

415
00:15:18,371 --> 00:15:19,918
That is a long run,

416
00:15:19,918 --> 00:15:21,953
but according to V E H Q,

417
00:15:21,953 --> 00:15:24,803
its sales stayed modest throughout.

418
00:15:25,153 --> 00:15:27,083
The second is its cousin,

419
00:15:27,083 --> 00:15:28,935
the Chevrolet Avalanche,

420
00:15:28,935 --> 00:15:31,714
sold from two thousand two to twenty

421
00:15:31,714 --> 00:15:32,409
thirteen.

422
00:15:32,589 --> 00:15:34,937
It had a clever folding midgate that

423
00:15:34,937 --> 00:15:37,155
let owners extend the bed into the

424
00:15:37,155 --> 00:15:37,546
cabin.

425
00:15:37,726 --> 00:15:38,969
Many owners loved it.

426
00:15:39,149 --> 00:15:41,378
But it sat between a pickup and

427
00:15:41,378 --> 00:15:42,026
an S U V,

428
00:15:42,026 --> 00:15:44,975
and when buyers moved toward regular crew

429
00:15:44,975 --> 00:15:47,492
cab pickups, there was no room left

430
00:15:47,492 --> 00:15:47,995
for it.

431
00:15:48,175 --> 00:15:52,055
The twist: crew cab trucks basically absorbed

432
00:15:52,055 --> 00:15:52,831
its idea.

433
00:15:53,181 --> 00:15:55,697
The third is the Hummer H two

434
00:15:55,697 --> 00:15:56,218
S U T,

435
00:15:56,218 --> 00:15:58,995
a pickup version of the Hummer H

436
00:15:58,995 --> 00:16:02,033
two, sold from two thousand five to

437
00:16:02,033 --> 00:16:03,595
two thousand nine.

438
00:16:03,775 --> 00:16:04,716
It was huge,

439
00:16:04,716 --> 00:16:06,443
thirsty and expensive,

440
00:16:06,443 --> 00:16:09,425
and it arrived just before fuel prices

441
00:16:09,425 --> 00:16:12,250
spiked and the financial crisis hit.

442
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:15,595
When General Motors went through bankruptcy in

443
00:16:15,595 --> 00:16:16,834
two thousand nine,

444
00:16:16,834 --> 00:16:18,966
the Hummer brand was shut down.

445
00:16:19,146 --> 00:16:21,602
Timing can kill a truck as surely

446
00:16:21,602 --> 00:16:22,792
as a bad design.

447
00:16:23,142 --> 00:16:24,082
And the twist?

448
00:16:24,262 --> 00:16:27,029
The Hummer name came back in twenty

449
00:16:27,029 --> 00:16:29,638
twenty-one as an electric pickup,

450
00:16:29,638 --> 00:16:31,298
the G M C Hummer E V.

451
00:16:31,478 --> 00:16:33,916
A brand that died partly because of

452
00:16:33,916 --> 00:16:36,563
fuel prices returned as a vehicle that

453
00:16:36,563 --> 00:16:37,956
uses no fuel at all.

454
00:16:38,136 --> 00:16:40,864
The truck business has a strange memory.

455
00:16:41,044 --> 00:16:42,337
Names come back,

456
00:16:42,337 --> 00:16:43,629
ideas come back,

457
00:16:43,629 --> 00:16:46,780
and sometimes they get a second chance.

458
00:16:47,130 --> 00:16:49,803
So what is the pattern behind all

459
00:16:49,803 --> 00:16:50,775
seven flops?

460
00:16:50,955 --> 00:16:52,139
There are three.

461
00:16:52,319 --> 00:16:53,562
First, price.

462
00:16:53,742 --> 00:16:55,456
The Blackwood, the Baja,

463
00:16:55,456 --> 00:16:58,098
the Santa Cruz and the Cybertruck all

464
00:16:58,098 --> 00:17:01,027
cost more than the trucks buyers compared

465
00:17:01,027 --> 00:17:01,741
them with.

466
00:17:01,921 --> 00:17:04,034
Second, practicality.

467
00:17:04,214 --> 00:17:06,743
Trucks without four-wheel drive,

468
00:17:06,743 --> 00:17:07,928
with tiny beds,

469
00:17:07,928 --> 00:17:11,247
or with limited towing range were rejected

470
00:17:11,247 --> 00:17:14,013
by buyers who use trucks as trucks.

471
00:17:14,363 --> 00:17:16,383
And third, loyalty.

472
00:17:16,563 --> 00:17:18,864
The Nissan Titan was a good truck,

473
00:17:18,864 --> 00:17:21,097
but it could not pull buyers away

474
00:17:21,097 --> 00:17:23,939
from brands their families had trusted for

475
00:17:23,939 --> 00:17:24,481
decades.

476
00:17:24,661 --> 00:17:26,848
Every flop on this list broke at

477
00:17:26,848 --> 00:17:28,967
least one of those three rules,

478
00:17:28,967 --> 00:17:31,017
and most broke two or three of

479
00:17:31,017 --> 00:17:32,521
them at the same time.

480
00:17:32,871 --> 00:17:34,763
And here is the final twist.

481
00:17:34,943 --> 00:17:37,189
Some of these flops paved the way

482
00:17:37,189 --> 00:17:38,414
for later success.

483
00:17:38,594 --> 00:17:40,969
The Baja and the El Camino idea

484
00:17:40,969 --> 00:17:42,960
came back as the Maverick.

485
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:45,347
The luxury truck idea lives on in

486
00:17:45,347 --> 00:17:47,354
the King Ranch and the Denali.

487
00:17:47,534 --> 00:17:50,622
The electric truck idea is coming back

488
00:17:50,622 --> 00:17:52,817
as a range-extended hybrid.

489
00:17:52,997 --> 00:17:54,549
In the truck business,

490
00:17:54,549 --> 00:17:56,737
a failure is often just an idea

491
00:17:56,737 --> 00:17:59,066
that arrived at the wrong time or

492
00:17:59,066 --> 00:18:00,195
the wrong price.

493
00:18:00,545 --> 00:18:02,834
There is a warning sign that many

494
00:18:02,834 --> 00:18:05,679
of these flops shared before they failed:

495
00:18:05,679 --> 00:18:06,373
discounts.

496
00:18:06,553 --> 00:18:09,131
When a truck needs big cash rebates

497
00:18:09,131 --> 00:18:10,457
soon after launch,

498
00:18:10,457 --> 00:18:13,403
it often means buyers are not convinced.

499
00:18:13,583 --> 00:18:17,224
According to CarEdge's October twenty twenty-six deal

500
00:18:17,224 --> 00:18:20,866
list, a twenty twenty-five Ford F-one-fifty Lightning

501
00:18:20,866 --> 00:18:23,683
carried eight thousand dollars cash back.

502
00:18:23,863 --> 00:18:26,479
Big discounts can be a great deal,

503
00:18:26,479 --> 00:18:28,786
but they can also be a signal.

504
00:18:29,136 --> 00:18:32,025
Another warning sign is a long list

505
00:18:32,025 --> 00:18:32,851
of delays.

506
00:18:33,031 --> 00:18:34,811
The Ram R E V was pushed

507
00:18:34,811 --> 00:18:38,000
back several times before it was cancelled.

508
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:40,103
When a truck keeps slipping,

509
00:18:40,103 --> 00:18:42,782
the company is often struggling to make

510
00:18:42,782 --> 00:18:43,950
the numbers work.

511
00:18:44,130 --> 00:18:46,512
Buyers who put down deposits on delayed

512
00:18:46,512 --> 00:18:48,711
trucks should always know how to get

513
00:18:48,711 --> 00:18:49,749
their money back.

514
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:52,105
And the last sign is a truck

515
00:18:52,105 --> 00:18:54,898
that tries to do something nobody asked

516
00:18:54,898 --> 00:18:55,185
for.

517
00:18:55,365 --> 00:18:57,883
The Blackwood, the S S R and

518
00:18:57,883 --> 00:19:01,391
the Baja all solved problems most truck

519
00:19:01,391 --> 00:19:03,190
buyers did not have.

520
00:19:03,370 --> 00:19:05,387
The trucks that succeed,

521
00:19:05,387 --> 00:19:06,900
like the Maverick,

522
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:10,765
solve problems that millions of people already

523
00:19:10,765 --> 00:19:14,295
have: price, fuel and everyday usefulness.

524
00:19:14,645 --> 00:19:16,530
So how do you avoid buying the

525
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,604
next flop in twenty twenty-seven?

526
00:19:18,784 --> 00:19:21,516
First, check the sales trend of the

527
00:19:21,516 --> 00:19:22,452
exact model.

528
00:19:22,632 --> 00:19:25,604
A truck whose sales are falling fast,

529
00:19:25,604 --> 00:19:28,656
like the Santa Cruz or the Cybertruck,

530
00:19:28,656 --> 00:19:30,504
may face discounts now,

531
00:19:30,504 --> 00:19:32,431
but weaker resale later.

532
00:19:32,611 --> 00:19:34,946
Second, check whether it is still going

533
00:19:34,946 --> 00:19:35,665
to be built.

534
00:19:35,845 --> 00:19:39,188
A discontinued truck can lose value quickly.

535
00:19:39,539 --> 00:19:43,361
Third, compare it with the best-selling truck

536
00:19:43,361 --> 00:19:44,466
in its class,

537
00:19:44,466 --> 00:19:46,419
on price, fuel economy,

538
00:19:46,419 --> 00:19:48,118
bed size and towing.

539
00:19:48,298 --> 00:19:49,995
If it loses on all four,

540
00:19:49,995 --> 00:19:52,893
like the Santa Cruz against the Maverick,

541
00:19:52,893 --> 00:19:54,661
that tells you something.

542
00:19:54,841 --> 00:19:56,768
Fourth, ignore the hype.

543
00:19:56,948 --> 00:20:00,435
Promises about future capacity or future features

544
00:20:00,435 --> 00:20:02,783
do not change the truck you drive

545
00:20:02,783 --> 00:20:03,566
home today.

546
00:20:03,916 --> 00:20:06,361
And fifth, count the full cost,

547
00:20:06,361 --> 00:20:09,359
including what the truck will be worth

548
00:20:09,359 --> 00:20:10,464
in five years.

549
00:20:10,644 --> 00:20:12,786
A big discount on a dying model

550
00:20:12,786 --> 00:20:14,513
can still be a good deal,

551
00:20:14,513 --> 00:20:16,448
but only if you plan to keep

552
00:20:16,448 --> 00:20:17,761
it for a long time.

553
00:20:18,111 --> 00:20:20,060
We put all of these checks into

554
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:22,827
the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide,

555
00:20:22,827 --> 00:20:25,027
with the numbers to compare and the

556
00:20:25,027 --> 00:20:26,725
warning signs to watch for.

